        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "refactor: remove browser and codex dead exports",
        "body": "Related: #105595\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nRemoves every remaining unused production export from the browser and Codex plugins so the shrink-only dead-export ratchet reflects code that is actually reachable in production. The original cluster contained 555 scoped findings; current `main` absorbed 39 overlapping removals while this PR was in progress.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nBrowser Playwright helpers now use one canonical export path instead of duplicate re-export chains. Other dead plugin exports and tests that existed only to cover them were deleted; Codex protocol-shaped surfaces were checked against the sibling Codex source, while plugin entry barrels and canonical protocol namespaces remain intact.\n\nThe TypeScript LOC ratchet initially inherited merge-order drift already present in `main`, blocking this and unrelated PRs. Main has since landed the broader canonical repair in #106042, so the final rebase drops the carried copy and uses main's guard unchanged.\n\nEarlier exact-base CI runs exposed unrelated QA Lab and iMessage type blockers on `main`. Those were fixed independently by #105983 and #106022; the final rebase incorporates both landed fixes without carrying them in this PR's diff.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo user-visible behavior change. Against current `main`, the dead-export baseline falls from 5,502 to 4,987 entries (515 net), with zero browser or Codex findings. The cleanup removes the remaining 516 scoped findings; one unrelated SMS export newly inherited from `main` accounts for the net difference.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `pnpm deadcode:exports:update` regenerated the pushed baseline after the final rebase; `pnpm deadcode:exports` passes with 4,987 entries and zero browser or Codex findings.\n- Browser suite: 138 files, 1,796 passed, 1 skipped; final CDP fixture rerun: 43 passed.\n- Codex suite: 106 files, 2,486 passed; final command-handler rerun: 148 passed.\n- Final Codex conflict rerun: dynamic-tool build 48/48 and TypeScript LOC ratchet 11/11 passed on Testbox `tbx_01kxcy2pem9g3a9992f0rxm73q`; the newly landed final-delivery behavior test remains covered.\n- Full production types, strict LOC, dead-export ratchets, and architecture passed on that same final Testbox. The earlier exact full guard shard passed, and the earlier Codex timeout conflict-resolution rerun passed 26 tests.\n- `pnpm check:architecture` passes, including zero runtime import cycles and zero Madge cycles.\n- Core, extension, and root test typechecks passed; the final full production typecheck also passed after rebasing the current Codex runtime changes.\n- Changed-surface format, SDK baseline, package guards, typechecks, core lint, and focused extension lint passed; four stale test imports found during the gate were removed and their 35-test rerun passed.\n- Fresh Codex autoreviews across the cleanup, ratchet repair, latest Codex conflict resolution, and final baseline reported no remaining actionable findings.\n",
